    "body": "The four work-process steps continually replayed their entrance animation while stationary. Their reveal clipped the same elements watched by IntersectionObserver, creating a leave/re-enter feedback loop.\n\nKeep each observed step unclipped and reveal only its children. The steps settle after entering, while deliberate viewport re-entry still replays the effect. Web 1 and other Web 2 content remain unchanged.\n\nValidation: reproduced 24 step animation starts in 4.5 seconds before the fix. Build and 11 unit tests pass. Chrome regression checks pass for all three Web 2 themes at 1536px and 390px, including stationary stability, replay on intentional return, reduced motion and horizontal overflow.\n",
